# A document taller than the window. What is drawn is a window onto it, and
# where that window sits is a property of the last drawing rather than of the
# document -- which is why the editor is a `var` parameter of a routine that
# only draws. Moving down past the last drawn line scrolls by one; moving
# back up scrolls the other way, and the first line comes back.
#
# The `~` rows are how a person tells a short document from a blank one.
# Seven rows and not six since the menu bar took one (ADR-0391): the window
# onto the document has to stay three lines for the claims above to be about
# scrolling rather than about a window too small to show a `~` at all.
name long.pas
size 7 12
push one
push two
push three
push four
push five
push six
draw
esc B
esc B
esc B
esc B
draw
esc B
draw
esc A
esc A
esc A
esc A
esc A
draw
